rpi
===

This crate family is a Rust port of the TypeScript `pi` SDK, not a verbatim
copy of it.

Upstream project
----------------

    pi — https://github.com/earendil-works/pi
    Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
    Licensed under the MIT License.

The `rpi-*` crates re-implement the original MIT-licensed TypeScript SDK in
Rust. The license text in `LICENSE` therefore carries both the upstream
copyright notice and the notice for the Rust port, as required by the MIT
License's retention clause.

Native provider catalog and wire-protocol adaptations
----------------------------------------------------

    Oh My Pi — https://github.com/can1357/oh-my-pi
    Reference revision: 73d7521269a1212fc2b2790a2e8c08424496c953
    Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner
    Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Can Bölük
    Copyright (c) 2026 Stencil Labs, Inc.
    Licensed under the MIT License; retained in LICENSE.

The provider catalog data and native Rust protocol/authentication adaptations
follow this MIT-licensed reference. No OMP executable, JavaScript runtime, or
TypeScript provider implementation is loaded to execute these providers.

Third-party dependencies
------------------------

Runtime dependencies and their licenses are listed by `cargo metadata` and on
each crate's crates.io page. Vendored or copied source, where it exists, keeps
its original attribution in the file header.
